                      [("供给是生产者在每一价格上愿意并且能够出售的数量。", "Supply is the quantity producers are willing and able to sell at each price."),
                       ("价格上升，供给量通常增加，沿曲线延伸。", "As price rises, quantity supplied usually rises: an extension along the curve."),
                       ("生产成本上升使供给曲线向左移动。技术改进使它向右移动。", "Higher costs of production shift supply left. Better technology shifts it right."),
                       ("间接税使供给向左，补贴使供给向右。", "An indirect tax shifts supply left. A subsidy shifts it right.")],
                      "供给曲线向右上。生产者在更高的价格上更愿意多卖，因为覆盖成本之后的利润空间更大。天气对农产品特别重要：霜冻减少供给，曲线向左。\n\n和需求一样，先问变化的是自己的价格还是其他因素。其他因素才平移。企业数量增加也会使市场供给向右移动。",
                      "The supply curve slopes upwards. Producers are willing to sell more at a higher price because the margin over cost is larger. Weather matters especially for farm goods: a frost reduces supply and the curve shifts left.\n\nAs with demand, ask whether the change is the good’s own price or something else. Only something else shifts the curve. More firms in the market also shift market supply right.",
